# 23. SHARED WORKFLOWS WITH OTHER BUILDFLOW DASHBOARDS

The HR module must work as part of one connected construction management system.

Implement these shared workflows:

### Employee onboarding
HR creates employee → Documents submitted → HR verifies → Required approvals → Employee activated → Employee account becomes available.

### Attendance
Employee checks in with selfie and permitted location evidence → Supervisor reviews exceptions → HR reviews applicable exceptions → Approved attendance is shared with payroll.

### Leave
Employee submits leave → Configured reporting manager reviews → HR processes or approves according to policy → Site and project workforce views update.

### Employee transfer
HR initiates transfer → Required approval → New project/site assignment becomes active on effective date → Historical assignment preserved.

### Contractor onboarding
Contractor company registered → Worker details submitted → Documents verified → Required safety induction completed → Worker activated for permitted site access.

### Compliance
HR or Compliance Officer assigns requirement → Responsible person submits evidence → Reviewer verifies → Status updated → Renewal reminder scheduled.

### Payroll integration
HR maintains authorised employee and employment records → Approved attendance and leave data are made available to payroll → Finance calculates and processes payments.

HR must not mark salary payments as completed or bypass Finance approval.

